# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the sanitizer (ASan) build on Linux.
#
# When no X display is available, glfwInit() fails inside GLFW's X11 connect
# path (_glfwConnectX11 -> XOpenDisplay) and libX11/libxcb leave a few small
# allocations behind (4096 + 64 + ... bytes). Those frames inside libX11/libxcb
# show up as <unknown module> because the system libraries are not
# instrumented, so the only reliable anchor is GLFW's own connect frame.
# This is a third-party leak, not an Orrery one.
#
# Deliberately narrow: LeakSanitizer matches a suppression against every frame
# of a leak's stack, so this hides only leaks allocated beneath
# _glfwConnectX11. Leaks from Orrery code (even ones passing through glfwInit
# elsewhere) are still reported.
leak:_glfwConnectX11
